<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-8">
  <header class="border-b border-base-300 pb-8">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">Resume</p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 text-sm text-base-content/60">
      <a href="mailto:<%= Application.get_env(:sour_shark, :contact_email) %>" class="transition-colors hover:text-primary">
        <%= Application.get_env(:sour_shark, :contact_email) %>
      </a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/jflowaa" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="transition-colors hover:text-primary">github.com/jflowaa</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <span>California</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-12">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/50">Summary</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/80">
        Software engineer with experience building high-throughput, event-driven platforms end to end.
        Architected an integration platform from 0&rarr;1 at a lean, acquisition-stage company, and designed
        distributed compute processing billions of workflow steps per day in single-digit milliseconds. Deep in the
        .NET ecosystem with JavaScript and React across the stack; turns ambiguous product goals into shipped systems
        and stronger engineers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/50">Professional Experience</h2>

      <div class="mt-6 space-y-10">
        <article>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">
                Staff Software Engineer
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm italic text-base-content/60">Integration platform company (startup acquired)</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 marker:text-base-content/30">
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Zero-to-One IPaaS Architecture:</strong>
              Architected a proprietary Integration Platform as a Service from inception, taking the business from
              early revenue through acquisition and continued growth&mdash;on a lean cost base with company-wide
              headcount under 25.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Workflow Engine:</strong>
              Designed and built a low- to no-code workflow engine for defining event-processing and integration logic,
              executing user-supplied JavaScript in a secure V8 sandbox (and briefly C#); now runs ~4M invocations and
              handles over 1 TB of data per day.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Developer Ecosystem:</strong>
              Built OpenAPI-driven code generation, an SDK, and a CLI that let external developers build and run
              connectors on the platform, growing the ecosystem to 300+ public and private connectors.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Distributed Compute &amp; Event-Driven Systems:</strong>
              Designed a distributed NServiceBus architecture using the saga pattern to process tens of millions of
              events and billions of workflow steps per day in single-digit milliseconds, guaranteeing reliable
              ingestion and fair load distribution.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Backend Performance:</strong>
              Cut memory allocation 60&ndash;70% across the domain by reworking high-volume .NET paths to
              source-generated, streaming JSON deserialization instead of full-payload buffering, supporting APIs at
              1&ndash;3k requests/sec.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Database Design &amp; Optimization:</strong>
              Owned schema design and maintenance for a 16+ TB SQL Server database, reducing it to 8 TB through column
              compression, index tuning, and retention policies; migrated high-volume primary keys from int to bigint
              with coordinated rollouts to avoid outages.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Reliability &amp; Uptime:</strong>
              Sustained 99.99% uptime with no full outages by improving failure isolation and graceful degradation, so
              load spikes surfaced as latency rather than downtime.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Cloud Infrastructure &amp; DevOps:</strong>
              Operated Kubernetes workloads across AWS and Azure on Linux, with Prometheus/Grafana observability;
              introduced CI/CD pipelines and automated test suites from scratch where none existed.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Technical Leadership:</strong>
              Led the team as it grew from 3 to 7 engineers, owned day-to-day technical direction, mentored engineers
              through continuous pair programming and code review, authored RFCs and PoCs, and drove cross-team
              initiatives and architecture dependencies for organization-wide rollouts.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">AI-Assisted Engineering:</strong>
              Standardized LLM-assisted engineering across the team, using Claude, Copilot, Cursor, and OpenCode for
              agentic planning, research, code review, and test generation.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">Web Applications Engineer</h3>
              <p class="text-sm italic text-base-content/60">Industrial equipment manufacturer</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 marker:text-base-content/30">
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">API &amp; Database Design:</strong>
              Built high-performance REST APIs on ASP.NET Core backed by Azure Cosmos DB, using Gremlin for
              graph-based data modeling and queries.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Cloud Services:</strong>
              Shipped an automated reporting microservice on Azure Functions that let customers schedule
              equipment-data exports via email and MMS, surfaced through a React dashboard.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Testing &amp; Delivery:</strong>
              Established unit and integration testing practices and automated delivery with TFS and Azure Pipelines.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">Software Engineer</h3>
              <p class="text-sm italic text-base-content/60">Sports technology company</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 marker:text-base-content/30">
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Product Ownership &amp; Impact:</strong>
              Owned the core media and scoreboard product suite end to end as sole engineer, taking it from concept
              to market launch and early revenue within the first year.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Embedded Linux &amp; IoT:</strong>
              Built a resilient Linux media player that pulled scheduled S3 content (GStreamer/GTK), synchronized
              venues over WebSockets, and used A/B partitioning to recover automatically from power loss or failed
              updates.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Mobile Development:</strong>
              Developed native Android (Java) and iOS (Swift) apps for remote scoreboard control, team scheduling, and
              live game updates.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Engineering Standards:</strong>
              Introduced mandatory code review, coding standards, Git Flow, and CI/CD, reducing release friction and
              operational overhead.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/50">Technical Skills</h2>
      <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3 leading-relaxed text-base-content/80">
        <div>
          <dt class="inline font-semibold text-base-content">Languages &amp; Frameworks:</dt>
          <dd class="inline">
            C#, .NET (Core/Framework), Elixir/OTP (side projects), Python, JavaScript, React, SQL; working knowledge
            of Java, Kotlin, Swift, C/C++
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline font-semibold text-base-content">Cloud &amp; Infrastructure:</dt>
          <dd class="inline">
            AWS, Azure, Kubernetes, Docker, Linux, DevOps, Prometheus, Grafana, Nginx, Envoy, Ambassador, CI/CD
            (GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, TFS)
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline font-semibold text-base-content">Data &amp; Messaging:</dt>
          <dd class="inline">
            SQL Server (schema design, query tuning, retention and compression), Redis, Cosmos DB (Gremlin), SQLite,
            NoSQL, streaming pipelines, high-volume data ingestion
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline font-semibold text-base-content">Architecture:</dt>
          <dd class="inline">
            Event-driven and asynchronous design, distributed compute, workflow engines, sandboxed code execution
            (V8), OpenAPI code generation, SDK/CLI design, sagas, microservices, high availability, system design
            (RFCs/PoCs), REST APIs
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline font-semibold text-base-content">AI &amp; Tooling:</dt>
          <dd class="inline">
            Claude, Copilot, Cursor, OpenCode; agentic planning and research workflows, automated code review and test
            generation, Git (trunk-based/Git Flow)
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
